      "description": "ENDEVOR SME, with extensive knowledge and expertise in administration, processing, and support.\n\nDevelop, document, and enforce SCM Standards and Procedures, to ensure strict SDLC practices. \n\nAssist developers in resolving errors encountered during the promotion of code through ENDEVOR.\n\nAnalyze input component impacts due to changes to copybooks/dclgen during the release, to ensure critical programs are regenerated as required.\n\nAddress out-of-sync conditions, input validation errors, and footprint mismatches arising from changes to copybooks and DCLGEN.\n\nCollect and analyze statistics.\n\nMentor team members on the extensively documented processes and procedures. Including guidance, answering questions, and ensuring established workflows.\n\nEnsure that DEV and TEST environments are properly configured, maintained, and aligned with the latest release code, ensuring that the environments reflect the current state of the software being tested.\n\nManage database tables by emptying and loading data as needed. \n\nSupport data security initiatives such as data obfuscation, tokenization, encryption.\n\nStandardize Batch Control Cards, JCL, Proclibs and Runlibs.\n\nManage the Cloudframe Data-pops by stopping or starting them as necessary to reduce MIPS.\n\nCoordinate the cleanup of MQ after software releases. \n\nUtilize the CA7 job scheduler to create, execute, schedule, and monitor environment support jobs. \n\nIdentify/resolve issues related to environment support jobs, such as job failures, dependencies, and collaboration.\n\nCollect and compile IPE for SOX compliance on a quarterly basis.\n\nCollaborate with internal audit teams to review IPE, ensuring internal auditing standards.\n\nReview quarterly templates with external audit firms as necessary for their assessment of SOX compliance.\n\nResearch and analysis of issues related to the CICS.  Disable and enable transactions as needed.\n\nPerform mass binds and new copies for both batch and online programs within the CICS environment.",
